window.DH=window.DH||{};window.DH["e03"]={"id":"e03","title":"第三集","parts":[{"id":"p01","title":"Bree 的恐惧与婚姻困境","lines":[{"id":"e03p0101","s":"Alice","t":"After I died, I began to surrender the parts of myself that were no longer necessary.","r":true,"m":["surrender v.投降；任凭摆布，沉溺于；（被迫）交出，放弃；"]},{"id":"e03p0102","s":"Alice","t":"My desires, beliefs, ambitions, doubts - every trace of my humanity was discarded.","r":true,"m":["desire n.愿望，欲望，渴望","belief n.相信，信心；看法，信念，观点；信仰，信条","ambition n.追求的目标，抱负；雄心，野心；干劲","doubt n.怀疑，不确定","trace n.痕迹，遗迹；v. 查出，发现；追溯 every trace of = 一点一滴、所有痕迹、一丝一毫","humanity n.人类（总称）；人性，人的属性；人道，仁慈；人文学科","discard v.扔掉，弃置；"]},{"id":"e03p0103","s":"Alice","t":"I discovered when moving through eternity, it helps to travel lightly.","r":true,"m":["I discovered when I was moving through eternity 状语从句的主语和主句主语一致，且从句谓语动词含be动词时，可以省略从句的主语和be动词。这里就是省略了I was","eternity n.无穷无尽的时间；永恒，永久；永生；未来，来世；","travelling lightly helps 这会有用 / 这有所帮助 / 这样管用","It helps to do sth 做某事这件事有益、有帮助（it = 形式主语，无实际指代对象）","It helps sb to do sth. 它帮助某人去做某事（it 是真实代词，指代前面某个事物）","lightly adv.轻轻地；轻松地；容易地；不费力地"]},{"id":"e03p0104","s":"Alice","t":"In fact, I held on to only one thing -- my memory.","r":true,"m":["hold on v. 保留，继续持有（常与 to 连用）"]},{"id":"e03p0105","s":"Alice","t":"It's astonishing to look back on the world I left behind, I remember it all, every single detail.","r":true,"m":["look back on/at/to 回顾；回忆"]},{"id":"e03p0106","s":"Alice","t":"Like my friend Bree Van de Kamp, I remember the easy confidence of her smile, the gentle elegance of her hands, the refined warmth of her voice.","r":true,"m":["easy confidence 轻松自信","gentle elegance 温婉典雅 gentle文静的，温柔的 elegance 优雅，雅致；简练","refined warmth 精致温情 refined精炼的；有教养的，文雅的 warmth温暖"]},{"id":"e03p0107","s":"Alice","t":"But what I remember most about Bree was the look of fear in her eyes.","r":true,"m":["remember most about sb./sth.关于某人 / 某事记得最清楚的是…","most做副词表示最（程度最高） mostly表示主要地、大部分地（范围 / 比例）","I like this song most. 我最喜欢这首歌。I mostly like this song. 我基本上喜欢这首歌。（不是最喜欢，只是大体上喜欢）","fear n. 恐惧；担心 the look of + 情绪名词表示… 的神情/神色"]},{"id":"e03p0108","s":"Alice","t":"Bree had started to realize her world was unraveling, and for a woman who despised loose ends, that was unacceptable.","r":true,"m":["unravel v.（使）解开，（使）松开；弄清，阐明；崩溃，失败","despise v.鄙视，厌恶，看不起 despite prep. 尽管，即使；","loose ends 未完成的事务或未解决的问题 loose adj.未固定牢的，松动的；零散的，松脱的；不受束缚的，未拴住的；","unacceptable adj.不能接受的；不受欢迎的"]},{"id":"e03p0109","s":"Bree","t":"Rex, You need to get up.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0110","s":"Rex","t":"It's not even light out.","r":true,"m":["even 修饰否定，放在 not 之后，加强语气, 甚至还没…"]},{"id":"e03p0111","s":"Bree","t":"Please hurry, if the kids see you sleeping down here, they're going to start asking questions.","r":true,"m":["see sb. doing sth. 看见某人正在做某事 see sb. do sth. 看见某人做了某事；看见某人经常做某事","start to do强调动作的开始 start doing强调动作的持续性 大多数情况下可以互换"]},{"id":"e03p0112","s":"Rex","t":"Let them ask, I don't care anymore.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0113","s":"Bree","t":"Well, I care, they don't need to be burdened with our marital problems while we're working things out. The least we can do is try to keep up appearances.","r":true,"m":["marital adj.婚姻的，夫妻关系的= marriage problems","work things out 解决问题：通过努力、沟通和解决问题来达成共识或解决问题。","The least we can do is (to) try... 省略了to，当主语部分有do的某种形式时，作表语的不定式加不加to都可以。","keep up appearances装门面；撑场面；维持表面的体面（或状况）固定习语，up 不能丢","appearance n. 露面，演出；到场；外表；表面现象，假象；出现；起源"]},{"id":"e03p0114","s":"Rex","t":"Yeah, appearances, I keep forgetting about appearances.","r":true,"m":["keep + doing，表示老是、总是做某事","about 可省，不影响理解,但 forget about 更自然，更符合不把某事放在心上"]},{"id":"e03p0115","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, Rex, you look so tired.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0116","s":"Rex","t":"I didn't sleep, this damn thing is so uncomfortable.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0117","s":"Bree","t":"Well, why don't you move back upstairs and sleep in our bed?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0118","s":"Rex","t":"We're in marriage counseling, Bree, I think that would confuse things.","r":true,"m":["counseling 是不可数名词（动名词，表示咨询、辅导这个抽象行为），前面不加a/an。","confuse v.使糊涂，使迷惑；混淆 confuse things把事情弄乱；混淆事情"]},{"id":"e03p0119","s":"Bree","t":"It's just I miss you.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0120","s":"Rex","t":"I know you do.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0121","s":"Rex","t":"Of course, if I find I can't start getting some sleep pretty soon, I'll be forced to move back upstairs out of sheer exhaustion.","r":true,"m":["pretty soon 很快 pretty 此处是副词相当、很","be forced to 被迫","out of exhaustion 因为疲惫而无法继续下去 exhaustion n.筋疲力尽；out of + 原因 → 出于 / 因为","sheer adj. 纯粹的，完全的；程度深的；陡峭的，垂直的"]},{"id":"e03p0122","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, Bree was afraid of many things, but if there was one thing she wasn't afraid of -- it was a challenge.","r":true,"m":["be afraid of sth. 害怕某事 = fear sth."]}]},{"id":"p02","title":"Alice 提出举办晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p0201","s":"Alice","t":"The day on Wisteria Lane began like any other, with a cup of coffee and the morning paper.","r":true,"m":["begin-began-begun 开始 start","like any other 像其他任何一个一样 ≈ any other day","the morning paper 泛指晨报 this morning's paper 今天早上的报纸","a cup of coffee / a bottle of juice / a carton(box) of milk / a glass of water / a can of cola 一些表示饮料的量词"]},{"id":"e03p0202","s":"Alice","t":"And while Lynette read the business section, and Gabrielle studied the fall collections, and Bree searched for decorating ideas, Susan scanned the front page and saw something that caught her eye.","r":true,"m":["while只能接长动作，侧重两件事同时发生；还能表对比’然而’。","business section 商业版 (of the morning paper) 报纸栏目用 section","fall collections 秋季时装 fall/autumn 秋天 spring summer winter","decorate v.装饰；粉刷；点缀 decorating ideas 装饰灵感","scan vt. 细看，审视；粗略看，浏览；扫描检查","the front page 头版","catch one’s eye 吸引某人的目光；引起某人注意。固定搭配，不用复数 eyes"]},{"id":"e03p0203","s":"Alice","t":"Well, it's about time!","r":true,"m":["It's about time 怎么现在才来/是时候了/早该如此了/总算等到了"]},{"id":"e03p0204","s":"Susan","t":"Be nice, I come bearing snacks.","r":true,"m":["bear v.手持，携带；经得起；承受，容忍","I come bearing snacks. = I come bringing snacks. 前者更正式、更有文采","snack n.零食，点心，小吃；快餐；snake 蛇"]},{"id":"e03p0205","s":"Bree","t":"Lynette, these cards are sticky.","r":true,"m":["sticky adj.黏性的"]},{"id":"e03p0206","s":"Lynette","t":"I know, Preston used three diamonds to scoop jam out of the jar.","r":true,"m":["diamonds 方块 (梅花clubs 红心hearts 黑桃spades)","three diamonds，52(不加大小王)-3=49，更正确的说法 three diamond cards.","three of diamonds 方块3，固定搭配。打牌时简称 the three / diamond three 即可","Ace two three ... Jack Queen King Joker","scoop v.用勺舀，用铲子铲；挖出 n.勺，球形勺；铲，铲斗；","jam n.果酱；堵塞，拥挤；麻烦，困境；","jar n.玻璃罐，广口瓶；一瓶，一罐 a jar of jam 一罐果酱"]},{"id":"e03p0207","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Gorgeous, thankful we have 49 cards to play with.","r":true,"m":["Gorgeous adj.美丽动人的；令人愉快的；绚丽的，华丽的，相当于我们说漂亮！","thankful (that) 庆幸…;因…而感激 thankful adj. 感谢的，感激的","cards to play with 表示有牌可以玩，去掉with会有点奇怪，但play cards（打牌）是固定搭配"]},{"id":"e03p0208","s":"Susan","t":"Hello, sorry I'm late.","r":false},{"id":"e03p0209","s":"Alice","t":"So, Susan, I was just telling the girls I want to throw a dinner party.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0210","s":"Susan","t":"Really?","r":false},{"id":"e03p0211","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, how long have we all lived on this street, we've never done a big group thing.","r":true,"m":["we all = 我们所有人;在主语 + 助动词 + 谓语动词的结构中，all 放在主语之后，实义动词之前；有助动词时，放在助动词之后。We have all lived on this street.","a big group thing 大型团体活动","How long has it been since you lived on this street? （搬走了）搬走多久？","How long have you lived on this street? （还住着）住了多久？How long has it been since you moved onto this street?"]},{"id":"e03p0212","s":"Bree","t":"I think it's a great idea.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0213","s":"Alice","t":"Paul never likes to have people over, but the heck with him, I'm doing it.","r":true,"m":["have sb over 请某人来做客 have people over 邀请人来家里","the heck with him 去他的，管他呢 heck n.该死，见鬼","the hell with him 语气更强硬、激烈，带有更明显的负面情绪。"]},{"id":"e03p0214","s":"Susan","t":"So, when is this shindig?","r":true,"m":["shindig n.盛大舞会；热闹喧哗的社交聚会"]},{"id":"e03p0215","s":"Alice","t":"How about a month from tonight? That would be the 16th, good for everyone?","r":true,"m":["How about + 名词 / 动名词 (doing) / 代词？…怎么样/如何？","the 16th 指一个月中的第 16 日","good for everyone = work for sb 对某人合适、方便、可行"]},{"id":"e03p0216","s":"Bree","t":"Works for me, should we all make something?","r":true,"m":["Works for me. 我没问题"]},{"id":"e03p0217","s":"Alice","t":"Oh no, this is my party, I've been wanting to have everyone over for years. I'm so happy we're finally doing this, it's gonna be so much fun.","r":true,"m":["I've been wanting to do sth 我一直想做某事,been wanting 更强调一直惦记着的持续感和情感"]}]},{"id":"p03","title":"主妇们决定举办晚宴纪念 Alice","lines":[{"id":"e03p0301","s":"Lynette","t":"Hey, I know, her dinner.","r":false},{"id":"e03p0302","s":"Susan","t":"How could we have all forgotten about this?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0303","s":"Lynette","t":"We didn't exactly forget, it's just usually when the hostess dies the party is off.","r":true,"m":["exactly adv. 精确地，确切地；","hostess n. 女主人，女东道主；女主持人；","be off 取消了、不进行了、黄了 = be cancelled 反义词是 sth is on（照常进行）"]},{"id":"e03p0304","s":"Lynette","t":"I'm not being flip, I'm just pointing out a reality.","r":true,"m":["flip adj. 轻率的，无礼的 v. （使）快速翻转；快速翻阅，浏览；轻抛，轻掷","I'm not being flip 现在进行时的否定，being + 形容词描述当前的状态,强调我现在不是在随便乱说","I'm not flip 一般现在时的否定句，表达的是一种相对稳定的个人特质或属性","point out 指出、指明","reality n. 真实，现实；实际经历，见到的事物；真实感，逼真性；存在"]},{"id":"e03p0305","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Mary Alice was so excited about it, it's so sad.","r":true,"m":["be excited about sth 对某事感到兴奋、激动"]},{"id":"e03p0306","s":"Susan","t":"I think we should go through with it.","r":true,"m":["go through with 坚持完成某事：按照原计划，坚定地完成某项任务"]},{"id":"e03p0307","s":"Bree","t":"Really? Wouldn't that be in poor taste?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0308","s":"Susan","t":"No, it's sort of a way to honor Mary Alice, it was so important to her.","r":true,"m":["sort of 弱化语气:算是、有点","honor v. 纪念、致敬、尊敬"]},{"id":"e03p0309","s":"Gabrielle","t":"We could all use a fun night.","r":true,"m":["use a fun night 度过一个愉快的夜晚"]},{"id":"e03p0310","s":"Bree","t":"Well, good, because I have some new flour that I've just been dying to show off.","r":true,"m":["flour n. 面粉，（谷物磨成的）粉 flower","be dying to do 非常渴望拥有或迫不及待做某事 dying: die的现在分词形式;long to do 表示深沉的渴望、向往","show off 炫耀; 卖弄"]},{"id":"e03p0311","s":"Lynette","t":"I'm in.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0312","s":"Bree","t":"I'll make braised lamb shanks.","r":true,"m":["braise vt.炖；蒸 braised adj. 炖熟的；焖熟的","lamb n. 羔羊，小羊；羊羔肉；","shank n. 柄；小腿；lamb shanks 羊腿"]},{"id":"e03p0313","s":"Lynette","t":"I'm still in.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0314","s":"Bree","t":"So how many will I be cooking for?","r":true,"m":["will be doing 将来进行时，到那时候我要做多少人的饭"]},{"id":"e03p0315","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Seven, three couples and Susan, does that sound right?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0316","s":"Susan","t":"No, it sounds very, very wrong.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0317","s":"Bree","t":"Is there somebody you'd like to invite?","r":true,"m":["would like = want 的礼貌版、委婉版"]},{"id":"e03p0318","s":"Susan","t":"I have an idea.","r":true}]},{"id":"p04","title":"Gabrielle 通知 Carlos 晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p0401","s":"Carlos","t":"A dinner party? Honey, I may be working late. The Dillman proposal is a complete mess.","r":true,"m":["may/might be doing sth 可能正在做某事,表示对现在或将来正在进行的动作的推测 maybe adv. （不确定）大概，或许，通常放句首","proposal n. 提议，建议；提案；求婚","the Dillman proposal 名词作定语，表示迪尔曼这个客户/项目的提案","a complete mess 固定搭配:一团糟 mess n. 肮脏，杂乱"]},{"id":"e03p0402","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No, you promised to be home every night this week.","r":true,"m":["be (at) home 在家 stay (at) home"]},{"id":"e03p0403","s":"Carlos","t":"I'll try but I can't guarantee anything, this is business.","r":true,"m":["guarantee v. 确保，保证；担保，为……作保；保修，包换"]},{"id":"e03p0404","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Says the prince as he rides off into the sunset. Boy, the movies ever get that wrong!","r":true,"m":["says the prince == the prince says 王子说着，倒装句，强调当时的一种场景","as一边… 一边…，两个动作同时发生、伴随进行，用 when 可行，当更强调当...时候，没有as贴切","ride off into the sunset 是固定习语，意为策马奔向夕阳，象征潇洒离去、圆满结局","sunset n. 日落，傍晚；晚霞;强调太阳落下的过程和景象 sundown 强调太阳落山的那个时间点","boy 是一个感叹词，哎呀、好家伙","ever 加强语气，相当于可真是、到底"]},{"id":"e03p0405","s":"Carlos","t":"You know what your problem is? You're very tense, you should go to a spa or go shopping, find a way to relax.","r":true,"m":["tense adj. 紧张的，焦虑的；= nervous"]},{"id":"e03p0406","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Where are you?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0407","s":"John","t":"Algebra.","r":true,"m":["Algebra n. 代数；代数学"]},{"id":"e03p0408","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Are you free at 4:00?","r":true,"m":["be free 有空 free 空闲的、有空的"]},{"id":"e03p0409","s":"John","t":"I'm not sure, I’ve got track after school.","r":true,"m":["I’ve got track after school. ==  I have track after school.","I have = I have got = I've got = I got（直接省略 've，口语不正式）我有…… 安排。","track n. 田径运动; 小道，小径；踪迹 track and field（田径）的简称"]},{"id":"e03p0410","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, get here as fast as you can, my husband says I need to relax.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0411","s":"John","t":"You want me to keep my gym clothes on like last time?","r":true,"m":["gym clothes 运动服、健身服"]},{"id":"e03p0412","s":"Gabrielle","t":"If you would, please.","r":true,"m":["If you would, please. 礼貌地请求别人做某事，如果你愿意的话，麻烦（做某事）"]}]},{"id":"p05","title":"Lynette 通知 Tom 晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p0501","s":"Tom","t":"A dinner party?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0502","s":"Lynette","t":"Yeah, it'll be fun. Bree's cooking, everyone's coming.","r":true,"m":["will/would will会表示更肯定，would会表示更假设"]},{"id":"e03p0503","s":"Tom","t":"You know what? I haven't even had a chance to unpack yet, honey, I just need to chill out for the next few days.","r":true,"m":["unpack v. 打开包裹；分析；卸下……；解除……的负担","chill out 冷静下来：指平静下来，放松下来。chill n. 寒冷；着凉 v.（使）冷却，冰镇 adj. 冷飕飕的；令人紧张的","for the next few days 在接下来的几天里"]},{"id":"e03p0504","s":"Lynette","t":"Oh, Tom, there will be liquor and hors d'oeuvres and grownups without children and silverware, remember silverware?","r":true,"m":["liquor n. 烈性酒；酒精类饮料；= spirits","hors d'oeuvre 法语词汇,指的是 开胃小菜；餐前小吃","grownup n. 成年人 = adult","silverware n. 银器；镀银餐具 silver n. 银；银器 adj. 银色的；银制的 v. 镀银"]},{"id":"e03p0505","s":"Tom","t":"Honey, can you take this in for me?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0506","s":"Lynette","t":"Have you heard anything I just said?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0507","s":"Tom","t":"Yeah, I'm sorry, I just, I'm wiped out. Three cities in six days, my head is just pounding, I'm not ready for a dinner party.","r":true,"m":["I'm wiped out 我筋疲力尽了 wipe v. （用布、手等）擦干净，抹掉","累：I'm tired. < I'm exhausted. < I'm beat. = I'm wiped out.","pound v. 连续重击，猛打 n. 磅（重量单位）；英镑 punch 用拳猛击、拳击 One-Punch Man 一拳超人 beat 打、击打、打败，最通用","my head is pounding 我的头正剧烈地痛着","be ready for sth. 为某事做好准备 be ready to do sth 准备做某事"]},{"id":"e03p0508","s":"Lynette","t":"I already got a sitter.","r":true,"m":["sitter n. 代人临时看管小孩的人 babysitter 的口语简称"]},{"id":"e03p0509","s":"Tom","t":"Can you cancel her?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0510","s":"Tom","t":"Please! Look, let's just stay in tomorrow night, we can get a bottle of wine and rent a video, and I just want to hang out with my best gal. That's all.","r":true,"m":["stay in 待在家里 stay at home","hang out with 与…出去玩,与…闲逛,强调和某人一起消磨时间 hang v. 悬挂，吊；垂下","gal n. 姑娘"]},{"id":"e03p0511","s":"Lynette","t":"I was looking so forward to a night out.","r":true,"m":["look forward to 盼望","a night out 外出之夜 a night in 居家之夜"]},{"id":"e03p0512","s":"Tom","t":"I know, sweetie, I'm sorry, but I'm beat. I mean, do you remember what it was like to work a 60-hour week?","r":true,"m":["sweetie n. 爱人，情人；甜的糕饼糖果","I'm beat 我累坏了 beat adj. 筋疲力尽，疲惫不堪 v. （反复地）敲，击，打；狠打，猛抽","what is/was ... like? …是什么样子的？/ 是什么感受？用来询问体验、感受、状况","a 60-hour week 每周60小时; 60-hour是一个由数词和名词通过连字符连接构成的复合形容词,常用于描述事物的特征、数量等(976 995)"]}]},{"id":"p06","title":"Bree 通知 Rex 晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p0601","s":"Rex","t":"A dinner party? Do I have to go?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0602","s":"Bree","t":"Well, given that we're hosting it, I'd say so. By the way, you won't be drinking at this party.","r":true,"m":["given that 考虑到，鉴于 == seeing as / since / because ","host v. 主办，做……的东道主；n. 主人；主持人；主办者；宿主；主机；","I would say so. 固定搭配，我认为是这样","By the way 顺便说一下","will (not) be + doing 将来进行时，表示到时候会处于做某事的状态"]},{"id":"e03p0603","s":"Rex","t":"Why is that?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0604","s":"Bree","t":"Because when you drink, you get chatty. No one needs to know that we're seeing Dr. Goldfine.","r":true,"m":["chatty adj. 饶舌的；爱讲闲话的；非正式的"]},{"id":"e03p0605","s":"Rex","t":"You know, if you spend half as much time working on our problems as you do covering them...","r":true,"m":["half as...as 是...的一半  half as + 形容词/副词 + as / half as much/many + 名词 + as","spend half as much time doing A as you do doing B 花在做 A 这件事上的时间是你花在做 B 这件事上时间的一半.you do 中的do代替前面的spend time"]},{"id":"e03p0606","s":"Bree","t":"Not a drop.","r":true,"m":["Not a drop 一滴都不准喝。"]},{"id":"e03p0607","s":"Rex","t":"You know, this is ridiculous. And this whole thing about us taking tennis lessons?","r":true,"m":["ridiculous adj. 可笑的，荒谬的"]},{"id":"e03p0608","s":"Bree","t":"Well, the nurses at your office may start wondering why you're disappearing three times a week.","r":true,"m":["一般现在时 + 频率状语 = 表达习惯性、规律性的动作","现在进行时 + 频率状语 = 强调这个重复行为是当前阶段的、暂时的、正在被注意到的现象"]},{"id":"e03p0609","s":"Bree","t":"Tennis lessons are a plausible alibi.","r":true,"m":["plausible adj. 似乎是真的，貌似有理的；","alibi n. 不在场证明或辩解；托辞 v. 辩解；找托辞开脱"]},{"id":"e03p0610","s":"Rex","t":"So these tennis lessons we're taking, how are we doing?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0611","s":"Bree","t":"My backhand's improving immensely, but you're still having problems with your serve.","r":true,"m":["backhand n. 反手拍；反手抽击","improve v. 康复，健康好转；超过，胜过；提高……的价值；改善，变得更好","immensely adv. 极其，非常","serve n. （网球、排球等的）发球； v.为…工作；接待，服务"]},{"id":"e03p0612","s":"Rex","t":"Of course.","r":false}]},{"id":"p07","title":"Susan 通知 Carl 晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p0701","s":"Carl","t":"A dinner party?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0702","s":"Susan","t":"It's tomorrow night, so if you could just keep Julie an extra day.","r":true,"m":["keep sb (for) an extra day 让某人多留一天 extra adj. 额外的；另外收费的"]},{"id":"e03p0703","s":"Carl","t":"Fine, but that's all, Brandi and I leave Sunday for a week up at the cabin.","r":true,"m":["we are leaving on Sunday 进行时=日常计划，一般现在时=照日程执行，更果断；省略 on 是美式口语习惯","cabin n. 小木屋；船舱","up at /down at + 地点 表示在某个地方，带有方向感；没有特别的规定，如果地点在北边/山上/乡下/远处 → 倾向用 up at；如果地点在南边/楼下/市中心/近处 → 倾向用 down at"]},{"id":"e03p0704","s":"Susan","t":"What cabin?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0705","s":"Carl","t":"Brandi wanted some place where we could get away. Escrow just closed yesterday.","r":true,"m":["get away 离开某个地方，逃脱：为了避免不愉快的事情或寻求休息和放松。","escrow just closed （房产交易的）托管手续办完了。 escrow 托管,代管契约；第三方托管的财物","在美国买房在付钱 → 拿钥匙中间有一段托管期（escrow period），买方的房款和卖方的产权文件都先交给一家中立的第三方机构（escrow company）保管。所有条件都满足后 escrow close（关闭）才算交易完成，房子真正到手了。"]},{"id":"e03p0706","s":"Susan","t":"You can afford a cabin, but you can't scrape up child support?","r":true,"m":["afford v. 买得起；有（时间）做某事；承担得起；<正式>提供，给予","scrape up 凑集，筹集 scrape v. 刮除；刮擦；擦伤；勉强维持；凑集，积累"]},{"id":"e03p0707","s":"Carl","t":"The check is in the mail.","r":true,"m":["in the mail 在邮寄中"]},{"id":"e03p0708","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, no, it's not.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0709","s":"Julie","t":"I found my dental guard, I'm ready. Stop fighting.","r":true,"m":["dental guard 护牙套 dental adj. 牙齿的 guard n. 卫兵，警卫 v. 守卫，保卫","Stop fighting. 停止争吵、打架或冲突的行为"]},{"id":"e03p0710","s":"Susan","t":"We are being as nice as we possibly can to one another.","r":true,"m":["We are being 这是be动词的现在进行时态,表示我们现在正处于…的状态。","be nice to sb. 是固定搭配：对某人友善","one another == each other 都可以表达相互的关系"]},{"id":"e03p0711","s":"Julie","t":"Like I said, stop fighting.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0712","s":"Susan","t":"Excuse me, Brandi, do you mind?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0713","s":"Brandi","t":"Oh, OK.","r":false},{"id":"e03p0714","s":"Carl","t":"Wait, Susan, you're right there, you can pick it up.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0715","s":"Susan","t":"I could, but she's the one who threw it.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0716","s":"Carl","t":"Come on, don't be petulant, just pick up the stupid can.","r":true,"m":["petulant adj.闹脾气的、使性子的；暴躁的；任性的；难以取悦的 反：pleasant 近：willful perverse"]},{"id":"e03p0717","s":"Susan","t":"No.","r":false},{"id":"e03p0718","s":"Julie","t":"I can pick it up.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0719","s":"Susan","t":"Honey, stay out of this.","r":true,"m":["stay out of this 别插手这件事;别卷入这件事"]},{"id":"e03p0720","s":"Carl","t":"Fine, this is so typical.","r":true,"m":["this is so typical 美剧里极高频的吐槽台词，太典型了/果然如此 typical adj. 典型的"]},{"id":"e03p0721","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, I'm sorry, was that petulant, too?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0722","s":"Carl","t":"You know what? You pick up the damn can yourself.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0723","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, well, you just go to hell.","r":true,"m":["you just go to hell 你去死吧"]},{"id":"e03p0724","s":"Mike","t":"You want me to pick it up?","r":true}]},{"id":"p08","title":"Zack 质问 Paul 不登讣告","lines":[{"id":"e03p0801","s":"Zack","t":"Mrs. Warmington said she looked for mom's obituary and couldn't find it. Did you put one in?","r":true,"m":["look for 日常查找，比较随意，带 search 的一些词组更偏向搜查的意思","obituary n. （报纸上的）讣告，讣文 adj. 讣告的","put in 登报、刊登、发布"]},{"id":"e03p0802","s":"Paul","t":"I've had other things on my mind, Zack.","r":true,"m":["I've had other things on my mind 我一直在想着其他事情","on one's mind 压在心上 in one's mind 装在脑子里"]},{"id":"e03p0803","s":"Zack","t":"But how could you not do that? People are going to think we didn't care about her.","r":true,"m":["care about 关心、在意、重视；对某人/某事有牵挂"]},{"id":"e03p0804","s":"Paul","t":"I doubt people will give it much thought, don't worry about it.","r":true,"m":["give sth much thought = 认真考虑某事"]},{"id":"e03p0805","s":"Zack","t":"You never talk about her.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0806","s":"Zack","t":"She hasn't even been dead a month and it's like you've totally forgotten she ever existed.","r":true,"m":["be dead 是用形容词来表示状态，处于死亡状态 die 是一个瞬间动作，后面不可以接 (for) a month","totally adv. 完全地，整个地；对极了，太对了","exist v. 存在，实际上有；持续存在，生存"]},{"id":"e03p0807","s":"Paul","t":"It's a little early for this kind of talk.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0808","s":"Zack","t":"Maybe when you die, I won't put in an obituary.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0809","s":"Paul","t":"That will be your choice to make, assuming you outlive me.","r":true,"m":["assume v. 假定，假设，认为；装出，做出；承担，就职；呈现，具有","outlive v. 比……活得长，比……活得久；比……经久；"]}]},{"id":"p09","title":"Gabrielle 的轶事被发现？","lines":[{"id":"e03p0901","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Mom, it's no big deal. Carlos and I are driving in for the baptism, problem solved.","r":true,"m":["it's no big deal 没什么大不了的; 这不是什么大事","drive in 强调开车前往（某个地方）/ drive up","baptism（洗礼/受洗）是基督教的重要仪式，有婴儿洗礼和成人洗礼","problem solved 问题解决了"]},{"id":"e03p0902","s":"Gabrielle","t":"OK, fine, you go with aunt Maria, and I will take Nana to church.","r":true,"m":["church n. 教堂；礼拜仪式；教派，教会"]},{"id":"e03p0903","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Take your clothes off.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0904","s":"Gabrielle","t":"OK, I got to go, mom, yes, right now, OK, you can give me directions later, bye.","r":true,"m":["direction n. 方向，方位；趋势，动向；指示，说明 give directions 指路","Excuse me, how do I get to the church? 问路的王牌句式"]},{"id":"e03p0905","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Hi, How was school?","r":true},{"id":"e03p0906","s":"John","t":"Got an A-minus on my biology exam.","r":true,"m":["minus prep. 减，减去； n. 减号，负号 adj. 小于零的，负的；不利的 A-minus=A- B-plus=B+","在某次考试/测试上的成绩，用介词 on","biology n. 生物学；"]},{"id":"e03p0907","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, let's see what you've learned.","r":true},{"id":"e03p0908","s":"John","t":"Who's that?","r":false},{"id":"e03p0909","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I don't know. Hey, you!","r":false}]},{"id":"p10","title":"Susan 向 Lynette 吐槽与 Carl 吵架","lines":[{"id":"e03p1001","s":"Lynette","t":"So did Mike say anything?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1002","s":"Susan","t":"No, but god, you should have seen the look on his face.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1003","s":"Lynette","t":"I'm sure it's not that bad, I mean, he's coming to the party, right?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1004","s":"Susan","t":"I left three messages. Oh, he's not going to come, big surprise.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1005","s":"Susan","t":"I did everything but foam at the mouth, god, I hate when I get that way.","r":true,"m":["I did everything but ... 除了…之外做了所有事，but是介词，当but前面的动词do的某种形式时，but 后面接不带 to 的动词不定式","foam at the mouth 口吐白沫，勃然大怒 foam n. 泡沫，气泡；唾液，汗沫","get that way 变成那样；变得如此"]},{"id":"e03p1006","s":"Susan","t":"It's like every time I get within 10 feet of Carl, I just become this monster.","r":true,"m":["every time 没有everytime这个单词","get within ... of sb 到达离某人…（距离）的范围之内,如 get within 10 meters of sb","within prep. 在某段时间距离之内；接近 adv. 在里面，在内部；n. 里面，内部","feet 英尺 1 foot ≈ 30厘米，说是成人的一只脚的长度，但这要换算的话，就是50 码以上的脚，太大了。6 英尺是一米八","inch 英寸 1 inch ≈ 2.45厘米，大拇指第一节指节的长度 12 inches英寸 = 1 foot","monster n. 怪兽，怪物；"]},{"id":"e03p1007","s":"Lynette","t":"You know what? It's not going to change until you resolve your issues with that man.","r":true,"m":["resolve侧重化解、了结（矛盾、冲突、情感问题）solve侧重解答、破解（难题、谜题、技术问题）"]},{"id":"e03p1008","s":"Susan","t":"What? You mean forgive them?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1009","s":"Susan","t":"You know, I've lived with this bitterness so long, I think I'd be lonely without it.","r":true,"m":["bitterness n. 苦味；苦难；怨恨 bitter adj. 味苦的；痛苦的，辛酸的"]},{"id":"e03p1010","s":"Lynette","t":"Honey, get a pet, see ya.","r":true,"m":["see ya. ya: (=you)只被用于口语"]}]},{"id":"p11","title":"Lynette 与 Tom 因派对安排起争执","lines":[{"id":"e03p1101","s":"Tom","t":"It's a business meeting.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1102","s":"Lynette","t":"It's a frat party.","r":true,"m":["frat n. 兄弟会 frat party 兄弟会派对"]},{"id":"e03p1103","s":"Tom","t":"Regional manager, corporate manager, head of sales.","r":true,"m":["regional manager 区域经理 regional adj. 地区的，区域的；","corporate manager 公司经理 corporate adj. 公司的；法人的；共同的","head of sales 销售主管"]},{"id":"e03p1104","s":"Lynette","t":"Margarita, cigar, sombrero.","r":true,"m":["Margarita 玛格丽塔（一种鸡尾酒名）","cigar n. 雪茄烟","sombrero n. 墨西哥帽；宽边帽"]},{"id":"e03p1105","s":"Tom","t":"Honey, what do you want me to do? Sit around in the hotel the whole time watching cable?","r":true,"m":["sit around 闲坐，无所事事","the whole time 一直；始终","cable n. 电缆；钢缆，缆绳；电报；有线电视"]},{"id":"e03p1106","s":"Lynette","t":"No, but when I say we've been invited to a party, don't whine about your exhausting 60-hour week. Put on your dancing shoes and take the mother of your children out for a good time.","r":true,"m":["whine v. 嘀咕，抱怨；发出哀鸣 whine about 抱怨","dancing shoes 跳舞鞋 shoe n.鞋 dancin' 是 dancing 的口语/歌词写法，撇号代表吞掉的 g 音","take sb out 带某人出去，通常指约会或娱乐活动。take sb out for a good time 带某人出去尽情玩乐","the mother of your children 孩子他妈"]},{"id":"e03p1107","s":"Tom","t":"Fine, you know what? You're right. Let's go to that party.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1108","s":"Lynette","t":"I can't, I already canceled the sitter.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1109","s":"Tom","t":"OK, we'll throw the next one.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1110","s":"Lynette","t":"Throw a dinner party? I don't even have time to wash my face. No, you know what? I'm gonna go to this one, you can stay home and babysit the kids.","r":true,"m":["babysit v. （孩子家长外出时）临时代为照看婴孩","Every morning, I wake up at seven. First, I wash my face. Then, I brush my teeth. After that, I have breakfast, and finally, I leave for work."]},{"id":"e03p1111","s":"Tom","t":"Fine, I can handle that.","r":true}]},{"id":"p12","title":"神秘小女孩 Ashley","lines":[{"id":"e03p1201","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle spent her morning searching for the mysterious little girl. Sadly for her, the mystery was solved a bit too quickly.","r":true,"m":["spend + 时间 + (in) doing sth. / spend + 时间 + on sth.","mysterious adj. 不可思议的，难以理解的；神秘的，陌生的；保密的 mystery n. 难以理解的事物，奥秘；神秘的人","sadly for sb对某人来说不幸的是 / 遗憾的是","a bit/ a little / a little bit 稍微，有点，可修饰形容词副词。修饰名词时用 a little"]},{"id":"e03p1202","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Hey, what's going on?","r":true,"m":["what's going on? 询问发生了什么事、出什么事了"]},{"id":"e03p1203","s":"Carlos","t":"Have you met Ashley? Babe, this is Sheila Bukowski, our new neighbor, they just moved into the Miller's old house.","r":true,"m":["Babe n.宝贝、亲爱的（称呼），婴儿，小孩；女孩；天真幼稚的人"]},{"id":"e03p1204","s":"Sheila","t":"My daughter left her ball in your yard, I'm so sorry.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1205","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No, no problem. Nice to meet you, Ashley.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1206","s":"Sheila","t":"She's shy, she doesn't say much.","r":true,"m":["shy adj. 害羞的，腼腆的；"]},{"id":"e03p1207","s":"Carlos","t":"Yeah, but I can see her little mind working away.","r":true,"m":["work away 持续工作或努力：持续不断地工作或努力。 mind work away 大脑不停地工作，小脑袋在转、在琢磨事情（强调在思考）"]},{"id":"e03p1208","s":"Sheila","t":"Nice meeting you. Come on, Ashley.","r":true,"m":["Nice meeting you. 完整形式是 \"It is nice meeting you.\" 用于见面结束时，回顾这次见面的愉快体验。","Nice to meet you. 用于初次见面时，表达对即将开始的交流的期待和友好态度。"]}]},{"id":"p13","title":"Rex 要求私人咨询","lines":[{"id":"e03p1301","s":"Bree","t":"Private sessions? I don't understand. Why do we need private sessions?","r":true,"m":["private sessions 私人课程；私人会议；私人时段","private adj. 私有的，自用的；私营的，民营的；私下的，秘密的","session n. 会话;一段时间，一场；会议，（法庭的）开庭；学年，上课时间；"]},{"id":"e03p1302","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Private sessions allow us to work on the personal issues of both partners.","r":true,"m":["allow sb to 允许某人做某事","work on 努力改进：致力于塑造、形成或改进某物。","personal issues 个人问题","partner n. 搭档，同伴；合伙人；伙伴；配偶，伴侣，情人 both partners 伴侣双方"]},{"id":"e03p1303","s":"Bree","t":"I don't have any personal issues, my only issue is that my husband wants to leave me, and how can I work on that if he is not in the room?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1304","s":"Rex","t":"There are things I need to discuss with Dr. Goldfine, and I can't have you here.","r":true,"m":["discuss sth with sb.  和某人讨论某事"]},{"id":"e03p1305","s":"Bree","t":"Why? I'm your wife. You can say anything in front of me. All we need is a few more sessions, and I'm sure we can...","r":true,"m":["in front of 在……的前部或附近"]},{"id":"e03p1306","s":"Rex","t":"Damn it, Bree, a few more sessions is not gonna fix us. This is bigger than that.","r":true,"m":["a few more sessions is... 这里日常口语用的is不算问题，但是正规应该用are. a few + 复数名词；a little + 不可数名词"]},{"id":"e03p1307","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Why don't we do it this way? Rex, you can take the first half-hour. Bree, you can take the second.","r":true,"m":["half-hour n.半小时 adj.半小时的","half an hour 固定短语，表示半小时。但当前面加了 the first 这个限定词，和 an 互相冲突，一个名词短语里容不下两套限定。"]},{"id":"e03p1308","s":"Bree","t":"And doctor, if what he is about to discuss has anything to do with adultery, prostitution, or internet pornography, I would really appreciate you taking a moral hard line.","r":true,"m":["has anything to do with 是一个固定短语，意为“与……有关”","adultery n. 通奸，通奸行为 adult n. 成年人或动物","prostitution n. 卖淫；滥用 institution n. 机构，团体；制度；建立；","pornography n. 色情文学 photography n. 摄影","moral hard line 强硬的道德立场/道德高压线 take a moral hard line 采取强硬的道德立场 hard line 强硬立场、毫不妥协","I would really appreciate you taking a moral hard line. == I would really appreciate it if you took a moral hard line."]}]},{"id":"p14","title":"Gabrielle 讨好 Ashley 被索要自行车","lines":[{"id":"e03p1401","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Hey, Ashley, remember me? We met earlier.","r":true,"m":["We met earlier.我们早些时候见过，相对具体的、较近的过去时间点。We’ve met before.我们曾经见过，模糊的曾经。"]},{"id":"e03p1402","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Wow, aren't you the little artist? What are those, flamingos?","r":true,"m":["flamingo n. 火烈鸟"]},{"id":"e03p1403","s":"Ashley","t":"No.","r":false},{"id":"e03p1404","s":"Gabrielle","t":"What a very pretty! It almost looks like they are kissing.","r":true,"m":["What a very pretty! 感叹句 完整的是 What a very pretty painting! 可以替换成 how 引导的感叹句： How pretty the painting is!"]},{"id":"e03p1405","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Funny thing about kissing, it's not just for husbands and wives. Sometimes we kiss our mom or our grandpa. Sometimes we even kiss our dog. Sometimes we even kiss people who are just our friends, kind of like a high-five on the lips, right?","r":true,"m":["kind of like 有点像，有几分相似 kind of 有点、算是 == sort of. a kind of 一种…","high-five 举手击掌","lip n. 嘴唇"]},{"id":"e03p1406","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Hey, Ash, I was at the mall and I saw this, I thought you might like it. She is Hawaiian, her name is princess Kahalua, and I think it means \"little waterfall\" or \"big pond\" or something.","r":true,"m":["Hawaiian n. 夏威夷人；夏威夷语 adj. 夏威夷语的；夏威夷的","waterfall n. 瀑布；瀑布似的东西","pond n.（人工或自然的）池塘；"]},{"id":"e03p1407","s":"Gabrielle","t":"OK, so we are good, right? Well, you enjoy your new little friend, and if there's anything else you need, you just let me know.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1408","s":"Ashley","t":"What I'd really like is a bike.","r":true,"m":["would like = want 的礼貌版、委婉版"]}]},{"id":"p15","title":"Bree 邀请 Zach 参加纪念晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p1501","s":"Paul","t":"Where did you find that?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1502","s":"Zack","t":"She used this to kill herself, why would you keep it?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1503","s":"Paul","t":"Because I thought we might need it someday.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1504","s":"Zack","t":"For what?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1505","s":"Paul","t":"Protection.","r":true,"m":["protection n. 自卫，保护，防护；保护物，护身符；保险；"]},{"id":"e03p1506","s":"Zack","t":"I want to talk about mom.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1507","s":"Paul","t":"You need to take your medication.","r":true,"m":["medication n. 药物，药品；药物治疗 take medication 服用药物，使用药物，此时 medication 作药物治疗、服药这个抽象概念时，是不可数名词","日常对话 medicine可能更合适；医疗专业领域 medication 更合适。"]},{"id":"e03p1508","s":"Bree","t":"Hello, Zack, I hope this is not a bad time.","r":true,"m":["I hope this is not a bad time. 希望没有打扰到你。/现在方便吗？I hope I'm not interrupting."]},{"id":"e03p1509","s":"Zack","t":"What can I do for you, Mrs. Van de Kamp?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1510","s":"Bree","t":"Well, I wanted to invite you and your father to a dinner party tomorrow night.","r":true,"m":["wanted 委婉过去时，用过去式委婉的表达我（本来）想邀请你…，给对方留拒绝的余地"]},{"id":"e03p1511","s":"Zack","t":"I'm not sure where he is right now.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1512","s":"Bree","t":"Well, I'm sorry it's such late notice, but well, we weren't sure that you and your father were ready for any kind of social engagement yet.","r":true,"m":["it's such late notice. 更多的表达是 short notice. 通知得太仓促、没给留准备时间","notice n.表示提前通知、事先告知时是不可数名词，表示通知、公告时是可数名词","it's too late to notice 现在才注意到已经太晚了 notice v.注意，察觉","such 是限定词，用于修饰名词或名词短语，而 so 是副词，修饰形容词或副词。","engagement n. 约会，约定；订婚；聘用，从事 social engagement 社交活动"]},{"id":"e03p1513","s":"Bree","t":"But we're sort of throwing it in your mother's honor.","r":true,"m":["in one's honor 为纪念某人"]},{"id":"e03p1514","s":"Zack","t":"Really?","r":false},{"id":"e03p1515","s":"Bree","t":"Yes, it's gonna be a casual night with the gang, we're going to eat and tell fun stories about your mom. Zack, are you OK?","r":true,"m":["casual adj. 休闲的，便装的；随便的，非正式的","gang n.帮派，团伙 with the gang 和一群伙伴 / 一帮人在一起"]},{"id":"e03p1516","s":"Paul","t":"Hello, Bree. I heard, thank you, but we already have plans for tomorrow.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1517","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, that's too bad, well, I should go.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1518","s":"Zack","t":"Thank you, Mrs. Van de Kamp.","r":false},{"id":"e03p1519","s":"Bree","t":"For what, Zack?","r":false},{"id":"e03p1520","s":"Zack","t":"Remembering my mom.","r":true}]},{"id":"p16","title":"Gabrielle 送 Ashley 自行车","lines":[{"id":"e03p1601","s":"Alice","t":"That night, Paul gave his son something to calm his nerves.","r":true,"m":["nerve n. 神经；勇气；神经紧张；鲁莽； v. 使鼓起勇气振作精神","calm one's nerves 镇定神经"]},{"id":"e03p1602","s":"Alice","t":"And the next day, Gabrielle calmed her own nerves by giving something to her new best friend.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1603","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Here you go! Top of the line, 3-speed, aluminum frame, handlebar ribbons, and a bell.","r":true,"m":["top of the line 顶级的，最好的：在一系列产品中质量最高的；最好的。","3-speed 3个变速档位","aluminum n. 铝","frame n. 框架，边框；","handlebar n. 手把；","bell n. 钟，铃；钟声，铃声"]},{"id":"e03p1604","s":"Gabrielle","t":"And you'll notice it's royal blue to match your pretty little eyes.","r":true,"m":["You'll notice... 引导注意力:你会注意到…，委婉地提醒你现在看这里","royal adj. 国王的，女王的，王室的 royal blue 皇家蓝：一种鲜艳的紫蓝色。","pretty little 多个形容词修饰顺序：观点评价 → 大小 → 年龄 → 形状 → 颜色 → 来源 → 材料 → 用途"]},{"id":"e03p1605","s":"Ashley","t":"My eyes are green.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1606","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yeah, well, you'll be cruising so fast on this, no one will even notice. It's all yours, hon, have fun. What, what's wrong?","r":true,"m":["cruise 口语里就是轻松飞驰、狂飙的意思 v. 缓慢巡行，兜风；乘船游览 n. 巡游","will be doing 将来进行时:将要做某事"]},{"id":"e03p1607","s":"Ashley","t":"I don't know how to ride a bike.","r":true,"m":["ride a bike 骑自行车"]},{"id":"e03p1608","s":"Gabrielle","t":"What? Then why did you ask for one?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1609","s":"Ashley","t":"Why can't you show me?","r":true,"m":["show sb 给某人看"]},{"id":"e03p1610","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, sure, one of these days.","r":true,"m":["one of these days 将来的某一天：在未来的某个时间点。"]},{"id":"e03p1611","s":"Ashley","t":"What's wrong with now?","r":true,"m":["What's wrong with now? 现在有什么问题吗？"]}]},{"id":"p17","title":"Susan 准备放下对 Carl 的怨恨","lines":[{"id":"e03p1701","s":"Alice","t":"After her talk with Lynette, Susan decided to take a look at her old photo album.","r":true,"m":["We need to have a talk.（我们需要谈一谈）== We need to talk. We need a talk.别扭，少用","take a look at... 固定短语搭配，看一看…；看一眼…","album n. 唱片，专辑；相册，影集，集邮册 photo album 相册"]},{"id":"e03p1702","s":"Alice","t":"And she began to see herself in a whole new light, and the picture wasn't flattering.","r":true,"m":["in a whole new light 从全新的角度 light n. 角度；光，光线；see sth in a new/different light 以新视角看某事","flatter v. 奉承，讨好；使高兴，使感到荣幸；使显得更漂亮；","the picture wasn't flattering. 这张照片并没有美化（如实呈现）"]},{"id":"e03p1703","s":"Carl","t":"Yeah, you've got Carl, leave a message.","r":true,"m":["You've got Carl. 你找到 Carl 了，你打对了。标准：You've reached Carl.您拨打的是 Carl 的电话","leave a message 留言"]},{"id":"e03p1704","s":"Susan","t":"Hey, Carl, it's me. I was hoping you would be there.","r":true,"m":["was hoping + would = 落空的期盼"]},{"id":"e03p1705","s":"Susan","t":"Listen, we need to talk, so maybe when you drop Julie off tomorrow, we could have a moment. It's important, give my best to Brandi, call me.","r":true,"m":["drop sb off 放下，送到：将某人或某物放在指定地点，通常指在途中顺便完成。","give my best to sb 代我向某人问好;请把我最美好的祝愿带给某人"]},{"id":"e03p1706","s":"Alice","t":"Susan was proud of herself, she was finally ready to let go of her anger, well, almost.","r":true,"m":["be proud of sb 为某人感到骄傲","let go of sth 放下，放弃：停止对过去的执着。/ 松开，放开：停止握住或抓住"]}]},{"id":"p18","title":"Lynette 叮嘱 Tom 照看孩子","lines":[{"id":"e03p1801","s":"Lynette","t":"The boys will be hungry at 5:30, so put the fish sticks in the toaster oven at 5 o'clock.","r":true,"m":["fish sticks 鱼条 stick n. 枯枝，枝条；条状物，棍状物；","toaster oven 小烤箱、台式烤箱 toaster 烤面包机 oven 烤箱（大）air fryer（空气炸锅） microwave 微波炉"]},{"id":"e03p1802","s":"Tom","t":"For half an hour, honey, I know, this is the third time you've told me.","r":true,"m":["This is the + 序数词 + time + 现在完成时 (have/has done)：这是第几次做某事的固定表达"]},{"id":"e03p1803","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, if the food's late, god help you.","r":true,"m":["god help you. 愿上帝帮你，是一句警告、威胁或深切同情的表达。固定用动词原形 help 不加 s，属于虚拟用法"]},{"id":"e03p1804","s":"Tom","t":"Beautiful, I don't need a pamphlet. It's not brain surgery, they're just kids, for god's sake.","r":true,"m":["pamphlet n. 小册子，活页","brain surgery 脑部手术","it's not brain surgery 这不是什么难事；没那么复杂。不用加 a, 这里泛指一类事，视作抽象概念"]},{"id":"e03p1805","s":"Lynette","t":"Preston, would you come here? Sweetie, you know our rule about eating cookies, right?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1806","s":"Preston","t":"Yeah, we can't have them after 5:00, 'cause sugar makes us hyper.","r":true,"m":["hyper adj. <非正式>（行为）兴奋的，紧张的 n. 宣传人员","'cause conj.因为（because 的非正式表达）"]},{"id":"e03p1807","s":"Lynette","t":"Yeah, but tonight, anything goes. Make sure you share with your brothers.","r":true,"m":["anything goes 任何事都可以：表示没有行为、着装等规则；接受一切。"]}]},{"id":"p19","title":"Gabrielle 教 Ashley 骑车","lines":[{"id":"e03p1901","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Don't look at your feet, look at the road, find your balance, it's all you, you're doing great. Stay to the right, watch the car! Are you OK?","r":true,"m":["foot n. 脚，足；英尺 feet 复数","balance n.平衡，均衡，均势","it's all you 这全看你了；都由你决定；全靠你了。把舞台、机会或责任交给对方，表示接下来是你的时刻","Stay to the right 指示性语句，靠右（边）走/待着，要表达靠右（方向）→ to the right ","Keep to the right / Keep right（路牌标准语,靠右行驶/行走）"]},{"id":"e03p1902","s":"Ashley","t":"Yeah, let's go again.","r":true},{"id":"e03p1903","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Honey, these heels don't have another block in them.","r":true,"m":["heel n. 脚后跟；鞋后跟；高跟鞋；","block n. 大块，一块；街区；大楼；栋，座，幢；障碍物，阻碍；","these heels don't have another block in them. 这双高跟鞋撑不了再走一个街区了。","have another ~ in sb./sth. 某人/某物还有足够的存量再撑一次~","I've been studying all day. I don't have another hour/page in me.我撑不了再一个小时了/一页都看不进去了","This old car doesn't have another winter in it.这辆老车熬不过再一个冬天了"]},{"id":"e03p1904","s":"Ashley","t":"What about tomorrow?","r":true},{"id":"e03p1905","s":"Gabrielle","t":"You won't be around tomorrow, 'cause you have school.","r":true,"m":["be around 在附近","have school 上学"]},{"id":"e03p1906","s":"Ashley","t":"I'm homeschooled, I'm always around.","r":true,"m":["homeschooled adj．在家自学的 home-schooled"]},{"id":"e03p1907","s":"Alice","t":"It was in that moment that Gabrielle realized this ride was far from over.","r":true,"m":["It was in that moment that... 强调句，正是在那一刻","far from over 远未结束"]}]},{"id":"p20","title":"Susan 与 Carl 再次争吵","lines":[{"id":"e03p2001","s":"Susan","t":"I'm coming, Carl, what are you doing here? I asked you to come tomorrow.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2002","s":"Carl","t":"You said you wanted to talk, it sounded important.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2003","s":"Susan","t":"Tomorrow, I'm in a towel.","r":true,"m":["towel n. 毛巾，抹布，纸巾； in a towel 裹着毛巾"]},{"id":"e03p2004","s":"Carl","t":"We were married for 14 years. I know what's under there. Come on.","r":true,"m":["时间段前的 for 常可以省略，但是如果时间段放在句首，或者为了突出时间很长，就不要省略for。正式书面也建议保留for。在否定句中，用 in 代替 for 会显得更地道。"]},{"id":"e03p2005","s":"Susan","t":"I'm not really ready for this. I was gonna have a whole speech prepared.","r":true,"m":["was gonna =  was going to 过去将来感：原本打算、本来要，表示落空的计划","speech n. 演说，发言，谈话；a whole speech  一整篇演讲","have + 宾语 + 过去分词 使某物处于某种状态/让某事被完成。get也有这样的用法，可以替换，但get强调变化的努力过程，have强调结果。","prepared adj.有准备的，准备好的；打算做，乐意做；提前准备好的"]},{"id":"e03p2006","s":"Carl","t":"Brandi and I have plans tomorrow, I suggest you wing it.","r":true,"m":["wing it 临场发挥、即兴应付 wing n. 翅膀，翼；","suggest 有两种用法，suggest (that) + 主语 + 动词原形，虚拟语气,谓语用should +动词原形，should可省略。/ suggest + doing sth"]},{"id":"e03p2007","s":"Susan","t":"OK, here's the thing, Carl, I was thinking about what happened in the driveway yesterday.","r":true,"m":["here's the thing 事情是这样的/是这样的… 万能开场白，引出解释的关键点","driveway 私家车道——从街道通到自家车库/门前的一段私人路面"]},{"id":"e03p2008","s":"Susan","t":"I don't want to live like that, I don't want to be that kind of person, and I just thought if the two of us, you know, if we had a nice, calm... I need an apology, Carl.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2009","s":"Carl","t":"What?","r":false},{"id":"e03p2010","s":"Susan","t":"An apology, for the way you ended our marriage, you never took any responsibility for your behavior.","r":true,"m":["responsibility n. 责任，负责 take responsibility for: 负起对…的责任"]},{"id":"e03p2011","s":"Carl","t":"I don't know what to say, Susan, the heart wants what it wants.","r":true,"m":["the heart wants what it wants 一切顺从心意。"]},{"id":"e03p2012","s":"Susan","t":"What does that mean?","r":true,"m":["美式口语里，does 弱化成 's 的现象非常普遍"]},{"id":"e03p2013","s":"Carl","t":"I fell in love.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2014","s":"Susan","t":"While you were married to someone else.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2015","s":"Carl","t":"The heart wants what it wants.","r":true,"m":["the heart wants what it wants 一切顺从心意。"]},{"id":"e03p2016","s":"Susan","t":"My heart wants to hurt you, but I can control myself.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2017","s":"Carl","t":"I don't want to go back to that ugly place, really, and if you do, I suggest that you get some help.","r":true,"m":["ugly place 丑陋的地方, 不愉快的境地","suggest 有两种用法，suggest (that) + 主语 + 动词原形，虚拟语气,谓语用should +动词原形，should可省略。/ suggest + doing sth","get help 寻求帮助"]},{"id":"e03p2018","s":"Susan","t":"You know what? I don't need an apology, I don't need anything from you.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2019","s":"Carl","t":"You're humiliating yourself.","r":true,"m":["humiliate v. 羞辱，羞耻。有两种形容词变形：事/物用 -ing（令人...的），人用 -ed（感到...的）——和 bored/boring、excited/exciting规则相同","You're humiliating yourself. 你在羞辱你自己。这里只是 humiliate 这个动词的现在进行时，不是形容词令人羞耻的","The experience was humiliating. 这里的 humiliating 是形容词，表示令人羞耻的"]},{"id":"e03p2020","s":"Susan","t":"No, you're the one who's been humiliated, why don't you see that?","r":true,"m":["you're the one who's been humiliated 你才是那个被羞辱了的人，humiliate 动词被动语态","You look humiliated. 你看起来很难堪。这里的 humiliated 是形容词，表示（人）感到被羞辱的、羞耻难当的"]},{"id":"e03p2021","s":"Susan","t":"You walked out on your family, people think you're scum, not me, so worry about yourself.","r":true,"m":["walk out on + 人 = 抛弃某人、丢下某人（不负责任地离开）","scum n. 人渣、败类；浮渣；泡沫；糟粕"]},{"id":"e03p2022","s":"Susan","t":"I'm OK with me, I can walk down the street and hold my head high.","r":true,"m":["I'm OK with me = I'm OK with myself 我对自己挺满意的；我接受自己的状态","walk down the street 沿街走：沿着街道步行前进。","hold my head high 昂首挺胸：自信地面对困难或失败，不屈服于挫折。"]}]},{"id":"p21","title":"Susan 意外被困屋外偶遇 Mike","lines":[{"id":"e03p2101","s":"Alice","t":"As the sun slowly settled on Wisteria Lane, an unsettled Susan racked her brain to find a way into her own house.","r":true,"m":["settle 的核心意思是安定下来、落定 太阳 settle = 落定（夕阳沉落）人的情绪 unsettled = 安不下来（焦虑、慌乱）","rack one’s brain 绞尽脑汁、冥思苦想 rack v. 折磨，使痛苦"]},{"id":"e03p2102","s":"Alice","t":"Lying naked in her shrubs, it occurred to Susan this could be the most humiliating moment of her life -- she was wrong.","r":true,"m":["lie v.躺；位于 过去:lay -> lain 现在:lying (lay v.安放，放置)","lie v.说谎 过去:lied -> lied 现在:lying","naked adj. 裸露的，无遮盖的；肉眼的；裸体的，","shrub n. 灌木(园艺灌木) bush 原始的灌木丛","It occurs/occurred to someone that... 某人突然想到… occur v. （尤指意外地）发生；存在，出现；（想法）产生"]},{"id":"e03p2103","s":"Mike","t":"Susan? Whatcha doing?","r":true,"m":["Whatcha [口语] what are you"]},{"id":"e03p2104","s":"Susan","t":"Locked myself out naked. And then I fell. So how are you?","r":true,"m":["fall v.降落，落下；跌倒，倒塌 - fell - fallen"]},{"id":"e03p2105","s":"Mike","t":"Good, I just got back, I've been gone all day, and I got your messages about dinner, and I would love to come if that invite still stands.","r":true,"m":["be gone 表示不在的、离开的状态 I've been gone all day 我一整天都不在。我出去了一整天。","would love 比 would like 更强的意愿 = want","stand v. 仍然有效、仍然算数；站，站立；忍受，容忍；"]},{"id":"e03p2106","s":"Susan","t":"It's a date.","r":true,"m":["It's a date 就这么定了；一言为定"]},{"id":"e03p2107","s":"Mike","t":"All right, I assume the dress is casual.","r":true,"m":["好吧，我想着装应该是休闲的吧。","assume 假定、姑且认为，是基于常理/经验做出合理假定 guess就没太多依据"]},{"id":"e03p2108","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, it's casual.","r":false}]},{"id":"p22","title":"主妇们参加晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e03p2201","s":"Susan","t":"Thanks for helping me break in, do you think it'll be hard to replace that screen?","r":true,"m":["break in 闯入; 打断; 开始从事; 磨合","replace v. 取代；替换，接替；更换， 赔还；把......放回原处","screen n.纱窗，纱门；屏幕，荧光屏；银幕；屏风，隔板；掩蔽物，屏障；"]},{"id":"e03p2202","s":"Mike","t":"It depends, if you nail it yourself, you might want to wear gloves or pants, pants wouldn't hurt.","r":true,"m":["It depends 看情况而定","nail v. （用钉子）钉住，钉牢；抓住；戳穿，揭露；n. 钉子；指甲","might want to do sth 你可以考虑做某事/或许你应该… -> could -> should -> had better -> must 语气越来越强烈","glove n. （分手指的）手套；防护手套","pants n. <美> 裤子；<英> 内裤，短裤；","sth wouldn't hurt 做某事也无妨；某事不会有坏处。是 doing sth wouldn't hurt 的简写"]},{"id":"e03p2203","s":"Susan","t":"OK, I know what just happened is funny in theory, but I'm nowhere near ready to laugh about it, so please, no jokes.","r":true,"m":["in theory 理论上","nowhere near 远非，远不是; 远不够，远不足; 远未完成","laugh about sth 笑谈、聊起某事而笑 laugh at sb./sth.嘲笑/被…逗笑 tease sb about sth. 拿某事打趣某人/ make fun of sth/sb 取笑、开涮、嘲弄","no jokes 不开玩笑；别开玩笑了"]},{"id":"e03p2204","s":"Bree","t":"Hey, where have you two been?","r":true,"m":["where have you two been? 你们俩去哪儿了？Where were you?（那个时候）你在哪？"]},{"id":"e03p2205","s":"Mike","t":"Susan had a problem finding something to wear. Oh, is that the kind of thing you meant?","r":true,"m":["have a problem (in) doing sth. 做某事有困难","is that the kind of thing you meant? 你是这个意思吗 mean--meant"]},{"id":"e03p2206","s":"Susan","t":"Pretty much.","r":true,"m":["pretty much 几乎,差不多 差不多一样"]},{"id":"e03p2207","s":"Lynette","t":"The kids are bouncing off the walls? I'm sure you can figure out a way to put them to bed, Tom. I mean for god's sake, Tom, they're just kids.","r":true,"m":["bounce v. 弹起，反弹；跳动； bounce off 弹开，反弹；从…弹跳出来；掂量…","bounce off the walls（因兴奋、精力过剩等）举止轻狂、欢蹦乱跳、躁动不安","figure out a way to do sth 想出做某事的办法；找到做某事的途径 figure out v.弄清楚，解决，计算出"]},{"id":"e03p2208","s":"Susan","t":"Hey, are you OK?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2209","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yeah, I went jogging today, and I think I just pushed myself too hard.","r":true,"m":["jogging n. 慢跑锻炼 v. 慢跑；轻推","push sb too hard 把某人逼得太紧 push oneself too hard 把自己逼得太紧/运动过度"]},{"id":"e03p2210","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, you were probably not wearing the right shoes.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2211","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yeah, that thought did cross my mind.","r":true,"m":["that thought did cross my mind 我确实有过这种想法 did cross 这里使用了 do/does/did + 动词原形：强调句式","cross one's mind 想到，闪过脑海 cross（动词）across（介词/副词）= occur to sb."]}]},{"id":"p23","title":"晚宴上Rex 与 Bree 婚姻咨询被曝光","lines":[{"id":"e03p2301","s":"Carlos","t":"So Gabrielle says that you and Bree are taking lessons three times a week. I'm actually thinking about playing again. I mean, it's such great exercise.","r":true,"m":["take lessons 上课","exercise n. 运动，锻炼；（一套）动作，体操；练习，演练；"]},{"id":"e03p2302","s":"Rex","t":"Mm, that it is.","r":true,"m":["that it is 的确如此；正是那样"]},{"id":"e03p2303","s":"Carlos","t":"And my drop shot could use a serious tune up. Think you can give me the number of your pro?","r":true,"m":["drop shot 吊小球、放短球（把球轻轻打在对方网前）","could use 更侧重表达愿望或委婉的请求，need 更强调实际必要的需求","tune up 调整 tune v. 调音，校音；调频道；调整n. 曲调，曲子","pro n. 专业人士，职业选手；专职教练； professional 的缩写","Think you can give me it? 口语化省略 = Do you think you can give me it?"]},{"id":"e03p2304","s":"Rex","t":"Yeah, I'll give it to you later.","r":true,"m":["give sb sth / give sth to sb"]},{"id":"e03p2305","s":"Carlos","t":"Well, what club does he work out of?","r":true,"m":["work out of + 场所 固定在某处锻炼健身，驻地在某处工作"]},{"id":"e03p2306","s":"Rex","t":"We are not really taking tennis lessons, Carlos.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2307","s":"Carlos","t":"You're not?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2308","s":"Rex","t":"That's a story Bree concocted to cover the fact that we're seeing a marriage counselor.","r":true,"m":["concoct vt. 编造；调制（食物或饮品）"]},{"id":"e03p2309","s":"Rex","t":"Bree, he wouldn't stop asking about the tennis pro.","r":true,"m":["wouldn't stop asking about 不停地询问关于……（的事情）"]},{"id":"e03p2310","s":"Rex","t":"Bree and I are in marriage counseling. Everyone knows our secret now. Did the sky fall? Has your life come crashing down?","r":true,"m":["counseling n. 咨询服务","come crashing down 崩溃，突然倒塌：指事物突然破裂、崩溃或失败。crash v. 撞车，坠毁；猛撞；破产，倒闭，暴跌","天塌是事件，问事件是否发生（过去时）；人生崩塌是状态，强调对现在的影响/结果（现在完成时）"]},{"id":"e03p2311","s":"Bree","t":"If everybody would please take your seats, dinner is served.","r":true,"m":["take one’s seats 就座","dinner is served. 开饭了：正式宴会或餐厅中饭菜已经准备好，可以开始用餐。"]}]},{"id":"p24","title":"新闻播报发现神秘木箱","lines":[{"id":"e03p2401","s":"Reporter1","t":"With the winds from the northwest at 4 miles per hour, it's currently 55 degrees.","r":true,"m":["northwest n.西北方，西北方向；西北部 east south west north","at 4 miles per hour 以每小时 4 英里的速度。at表示以（某种速度、比率、价格等）per hour 每小时","mile n. 英里 1 英里 ≈ 1.6 公里 4 miles per hour 缩写 4 mph ≈ 6.4 公里/小时 微风","inch food block:街区，不是标准单位，而是城市距离的模糊概念，80-200 米不等","currently adv.现时，当前","degree n.度，度数（温度）；（角的）度，度数；学位；程度；次数；","美国用华氏度（Fahrenheit）°C = (°F − 32) ÷ 1.8 这里的55°F就是13°C"]},{"id":"e03p2402","s":"Reporter2","t":"Now we go to Rich, live on the scene in Westbrook.","r":true,"m":["Rich人名:里奇","live on the scene 现场直播 scene n. 事发地，现场；事件，场面；风貌；场景","Westbrook 韦斯特布鲁克（地名）brook n. 小溪，小河"]},{"id":"e03p2403","s":"Reporter3","t":"A grisly discovery was made today in Westbrook when a chest was found in Rockwater Lake, discovered by a local area businessman and his grandson while they were fishing.","r":true,"m":["grisly adj. 可怕的；厉害的；严重的","make + 抽象名词 = 对应的动词含义 1.make a decision = decide 做决定 2.make a discovery = discover 发现 3.make a choice = choose 做选择","chest n. 箱子，盒子，柜子；胸部，胸膛","lake n. 湖，湖泊；rock n.岩石；礁石"]},{"id":"e03p2404","s":"Reporter3","t":"Investigators recovered a wooden chest containing what appears to be human remains.","r":true,"m":["investigator n. 调查者，侦察员","recover v. 寻回、查获、找回；恢复；康复，复原；","cover 覆盖 discover 去掉覆盖=发现 recover  重新覆盖=恢复、找回 uncover 掀开覆盖=揭露、暴露","wooden adj. 木制的；","contain v. 包含，容纳；遏制，防止……蔓延；抑制","appear to be 好像是；仿佛 ≈ seem to be appear v. 出现，呈现；看来，似乎；表现得…","human remains 人类遗骸，永远是复数形式，主语用单复数都可以"]},{"id":"e03p2405","s":"Reporter3","t":"Now, a police spokesman says the body was ...","r":true,"m":["spokesman n. （尤指男性）发言人，代言人"]}]},{"id":"p25","title":"晚宴上众人袒露尴尬糗事破冰","lines":[{"id":"e03p2501","s":"Susan","t":"OK, I got to break the ice here. So you're in counseling, big deal. You want humiliation? I'll give you humiliation.","r":true,"m":["break the ice 破冰，打破僵局；中文的破冰是后来从英文翻译过来的借译词","humiliation n. 耻辱，蒙羞；丢脸的事，尴尬的场合","You want humiliation? / You want to be humiliated? / You want something humiliating?","I'll give you humiliation. / I'll humiliate you. / I'll make you feel humiliated. /  I'll give you something humiliating."]},{"id":"e03p2502","s":"Susan","t":"I locked myself out of my house stark naked and got caught by Mike.","r":true,"m":["stark naked 固定搭配：一丝不挂、赤裸裸 stark adv. 完全地；彻底地","get caught 被抓住 catch -- caught; get被动强调动作的发生、变化，有遭受的含义，所以多用于负面或意外事件"]},{"id":"e03p2503","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh my god, when did this happen?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2504","s":"Susan","t":"Today, right before the party.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2505","s":"Mike","t":"What can I say, right place right time.","r":true,"m":["right place right time. 天时地利。"]},{"id":"e03p2506","s":"Lynette","t":"I think I can top that. Try getting thrown out of Disneyland for lewd behavior.","r":true,"m":["top that 胜过那个、比过那个 top v. 胜过、超过","Try + doing（祈使句）你倒是试试啊 try doing sth. 尝试做某事;试试...的滋味 try to do sth 努力去做某事","get thrown out of someplace 被从那里赶出去 throw out赶走、驱逐","lewd adj. 淫荡的；猥亵的；下流的"]},{"id":"e03p2507","s":"Susan","t":"What? When was this?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2508","s":"Lynette","t":"When Tom and I were first married, things got a little out of hand on Mr. Toad's Wild Ride.","r":true,"m":["be first married 刚结婚 first 最初、刚开始","out of hand 失去控制 = out of control","虽然at表示在某个活动场所，但on对于在游乐设施上进行活动更常用","Mr. Toad's Wild Ride. 蛤蟆先生疯狂飞车 toad n. 蟾蜍，癞蛤蟆 frog 青蛙"]},{"id":"e03p2509","s":"Rex","t":"You're kidding.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2510","s":"Lynette","t":"No, we got perp walked down Main Street, USA.","r":true,"m":["perp walk 游街示众：警察押着犯罪嫌疑人在公众面前走过 perp n.罪犯 perpetrator 的缩写","got perp walked 这里get + 过去分词表示遭遇/被施加某事","Main Street, USA 通常指迪士尼乐园内的美国小镇大街"]},{"id":"e03p2511","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, since we're doing true confessions, Carlos and I once broke a waterbed in Cancun.","r":true,"m":["true confessions 真心话,真实告白,坦白 Truth or Dare = 真心话大冒险","confession n. 供认，供状；承认，坦白；忏悔，告解；声明，告白","waterbed n. 水床；电热充水床垫","Cancun 坎昆，是墨西哥著名的旅游城市"]},{"id":"e03p2512","s":"Mike","t":"How did you manage that?","r":true,"m":["How did you manage that? 你是怎么做到的？比 How did you do that? 多了一层惊叹和佩服"]},{"id":"e03p2513","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, he used to have a thing for spiked heels.","r":true,"m":["have a thing for sth./sb. 对……特别着迷、有特殊的癖好/喜爱","spiked heels 细高跟鞋 spiked adj. 尖的 heels n. 高跟鞋"]},{"id":"e03p2514","s":"Carlos","t":"I'd just like to make it clear -- she was wearing them.","r":true,"m":["make it clear 表达清楚"]},{"id":"e03p2515","s":"Bree","t":"Rex cries after he ejaculates.","r":true,"m":["ejaculate v. 突然说出；射出"]}]},{"id":"p26","title":"晚宴后Mike 与 Susan 深夜闲聊","lines":[{"id":"e03p2601","s":"Mike","t":"You think we left too early?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2602","s":"Susan","t":"I was thinking we left too late.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2603","s":"Mike","t":"So, is Rex gone for good?","r":true,"m":["for good 永久性地；彻底地；不可逆转地 == forever"]},{"id":"e03p2604","s":"Susan","t":"I don't know, god I hope not. I mean, they've always been wound a little tight, but I've never seen them like that. Then again, who am I to judge?","r":true,"m":["wind -- wound v. 弯曲前进，蜿蜒而行；卷缠，缠绕；n. 风，气流；风向","wound -- wounded v. 伤害，使受伤；n.创伤，伤口；损害，痛苦","tight adj. 牢固的，不松动的；紧身的；拉紧的，绷紧的；严厉的，严格的","wound tight 像发条一样拧得紧紧的，引申到人表示精神高度紧张、绷得紧紧的","Then again 不过，话说回来，另一方面; 再一次，又一次","who am I to judge? 我有什么资格去评判呢？"]},{"id":"e03p2605","s":"Mike","t":"You mean people who live in glass houses shouldn't throw soda cans?","r":true,"m":["People who live in glass houses shouldn't throw stones. 谚语-自身有弱点的人不该抨击他人；people是复数概念，所以用live","soda can 汽水罐 soda n. 苏打；碳酸水"]},{"id":"e03p2606","s":"Susan","t":"OK, you've got to know that I only get that angry around Carl, he just treated me so badly at the end. I haven't been able to get past it.","r":true,"m":["get angry 变得生气（变化）；am angry 在生气（状态）","badly 修饰动词 treat 用副词，口语中说 bad 也很常见，但正式写作还是用 badly","at the end (of sth)在某个事物的结尾处：at the end of the movie（电影结尾）in the end 最终、最后（经过一番过程之后）","get past 跨过、放下、走出、释怀 past 介词：越过、经过 get through 熬过、挺过"]},{"id":"e03p2607","s":"Mike","t":"Maybe he did you a big favor.","r":true,"m":["favor n. 帮助，恩惠，善举 v. 较喜欢；偏袒；有利于","do sb a big/small favor 帮某人一个大/小忙 Could you do me a small favor and pass the salt?","ask sb a favor = ask a favor of sb 请求某人帮忙","Can I ask you a favor? 我可以请你帮个忙吗？ == Could you help me?"]},{"id":"e03p2608","s":"Susan","t":"What do you mean?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2609","s":"Mike","t":"Let's look at Carl as a starter marriage, you know, boot camp, preparing you for something better next time.","r":true,"m":["see sb as == look at sb as 把某人看作；认为某人是，look不及物，不能直接接宾语","starter adj. 起步时使用的，基础阶段使用的 starter marriage 初婚，通常指人们在年轻时期经历的第一段婚姻","boot camp 新兵训练营, 军事基地训练营 boot n. 靴子；猛踢；后备箱 camp n. 营地；兵营，军营；","prepare sb. for sth 让某人为…做好准备","gym shoes/sneakers  运动鞋 dancing shoes舞鞋 (spiked) heels高跟鞋 boots靴子 dress shoes 皮鞋 slippers 拖鞋"]},{"id":"e03p2610","s":"Susan","t":"Listen, Mike, about the whole seeing me naked thing, I just want to thank you for being such a perfect gentleman.","r":true,"m":["the whole + [描述] + thing …那整件事"]},{"id":"e03p2611","s":"Mike","t":"Oh, I wasn't a perfect gentleman, I might have snuck a peek.","r":true,"m":["might have done 可能做了某事；对过去行为的不确定推测或委婉承认","sneak -- sneaked/snuck v. 偷偷地走，潜行；偷带，私运；偷偷地做（或获得）","peek v. 偷看，窥视；微露出，探出 n. 一瞥，偷偷地一看","sneak a peek 偷看：偷偷地看一眼或一瞥。"]},{"id":"e03p2612","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, good night.","r":false},{"id":"e03p2613","s":"Mike","t":"And for what it's worth, Wow.","r":true,"m":["for what it's worth 无论如何；不论其价值如何；通常用于引出自己的观点，并暗示该观点不一定有很大价值，但还是说出来供对方参考。"]}]},{"id":"p27","title":"晚宴后Lynette 和 Tom 聊 Bree 夫妻矛盾","lines":[{"id":"e03p2701","s":"Lynette","t":"How was your night?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2702","s":"Tom","t":"We are raising little terrorists. You know that, don't you?","r":true,"m":["terrorist n. 恐怖主义者，恐怖分子 adj. 恐怖主义者的，恐怖分子的"]},{"id":"e03p2703","s":"Lynette","t":"Oh, you didn't have a good time?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2704","s":"Tom","t":"You know what? Drop the act, I know you gave them cookies.","r":true,"m":["Drop the act 别演了。别再装了"]},{"id":"e03p2705","s":"Lynette","t":"Oh, who cracked, anyway?","r":true,"m":["crack v. 破裂，裂开；崩溃，垮掉；说漏嘴；屈服","who cracked 谁先绷不住了？/ 谁招供了？/ 谁破防了？"]},{"id":"e03p2706","s":"Tom","t":"Porter. So how was your dinner party?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2707","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, there was dinner, but it wasn't much of a party.","r":true,"m":["not much of a... 常用短语，算不上…的；称不上是…的"]},{"id":"e03p2708","s":"Tom","t":"Oh, what happened?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2709","s":"Lynette","t":"I don't know, Rex announced that he and Bree are in counseling.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2710","s":"Lynette","t":"She retaliated with this whole revelation which I won't even go into now, and the bottom line is he stormed out.","r":true,"m":["她用一整套爆料来反击——具体内容我现在就不细说了——总之结果就是他愤然离场。","retaliate v. 报复，反击； retaliate with + n. 以报复手段回应","revelation n. 被揭示的真相/内情；揭露；爆料 reveal v. 揭示；表明","go into 详细讨论、深入展开","the bottom line 最终结果，基本底线","storm out 愤然离场、怒气冲冲地走出去","retaliate 是以牙还牙，revelation 是掀开底牌，go into 是展开细节，bottom line 是最终结论，storm out 是风暴退场——五个词串起一场完整冲突。"]},{"id":"e03p2711","s":"Lynette","t":"Clearly, there's trouble in paradise.","r":true,"m":["paradise n. 天堂，天国 trouble in paradise 固定搭配（看似完美的关系 / 生活中）出现了问题、出现裂痕"]},{"id":"e03p2712","s":"Tom","t":"Honestly, I'm not that surprised.","r":true,"m":["honestly 说实话、老实说、说真的"]},{"id":"e03p2713","s":"Lynette","t":"Why not?","r":false},{"id":"e03p2714","s":"Tom","t":"I don't know, I just never got the idea that they were really happy.","r":true,"m":["get the idea that 产生…的印象/感觉/念头;感觉到","I just never thought/felt that ...; It never seemed to me that...(got the idea（最含蓄）< seemed to me < felt < thought（最直接）)"]},{"id":"e03p2715","s":"Lynette","t":"Are we happy?","r":false}]},{"id":"p28","title":"晚宴后 Carlos 谈论 Rex 出走","lines":[{"id":"e03p2801","s":"Carlos","t":"Man, oh, man, I keep seeing that look on Rex's face, and then him taking off like that.","r":true,"m":["Man, oh, man, 哎呀呀；天哪；好家伙","keep seeing 这里指脑子里不断浮现某个场景或事件，描述一个挥之不去的画面","take off 突然离开、抽身走人；起飞；脱下","see him taking off 省略了重复的 see"]},{"id":"e03p2802","s":"Carlos","t":"Some night.","r":true,"m":["Some + 名词（独立成句）真是……的一夜/一天/一次经历啊,带疲惫、感慨、不可思议的语气 Some night/Some day/Some experience"]},{"id":"e03p2803","s":"Carlos","t":"Then again, I would probably cry, too, if I had to have sex with that woman.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2804","s":"Carlos","t":"I mean, you watch a man get torn down like that, it makes you wonder why he let her get away with it.","r":true,"m":["watch sb. do sth 强调观看某人做某事的全过程 see/hear用法相同","watch sb. doing sth. 表示观看某人正在做某事，强调动作正在进行中","get torn down 被摧毁 tear v. 撕碎，撕裂；划破 n. 眼泪 tear down 是拆房子，用在人身上就是拆尊严","it makes you wonder why... 这让你不禁想知道为什么…","get away with 做了坏事却不受惩罚/不被追究"]},{"id":"e03p2805","s":"Carlos","t":"Believe me, if a woman ever humiliated me like that in public, Hm, it would only happen once.","r":true,"m":["这里是虚拟句，对现在的虚拟，因为说话人认为这种情况不太可能发生","ever 在这里表示万一、要是有一天，加强假设的不确定性；ever 的核心义只有一个：在任何时候（at any time）","in public 公开地，在公共场合"]}]},{"id":"p29","title":"Rex 决意离家","lines":[{"id":"e03p2901","s":"Bree","t":"So where are you going?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2902","s":"Rex","t":"I'll be staying at the motor lodge.","r":true,"m":["motor lodge = motor hotel (motel)汽车旅馆 motor n. 发动机，马达；汽车 lodge n. 门口小屋，门房；"]},{"id":"e03p2903","s":"Bree","t":"The hotel by the interstate has better rates, and it's closer to your work.","r":true,"m":["interstate adj. 州际的；州与州之间的 the interstate 州际公路,国家高速公路 by 表示紧邻、在旁边 interstellar adj. 星际的，恒星之间的","rate n.速度，速率；率；价格；rate 在酒店/服务语境中 = 价格、收费标准 better rates 更优惠的价格；更划算的费率","be close to 靠近、接近 close 结尾是s音 adj.近的、亲近的 close 结尾是z音 v.关闭"]},{"id":"e03p2904","s":"Rex","t":"Fine.","r":false},{"id":"e03p2905","s":"Bree","t":"I'm packing your swimsuit. There's a pool there, and I know how swimming relaxes you.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2906","s":"Rex","t":"When our kids ask where I am, what are you gonna say?","r":true},{"id":"e03p2907","s":"Bree","t":"I could tell them that you went to a tennis camp, that was a joke.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2908","s":"Rex","t":"Yeah, I got it.","r":false},{"id":"e03p2909","s":"Bree","t":"Obviously, if you've forgotten anything, you can come right back and get it.","r":true,"m":["obviously adv. （用于强调）显然，显而易见；明显地","have forgotten 到现在为止，你有没有落下什么东西？条件指向到现在为止是否已经发生 → 现在完成时","forget 如果你（之后）发现有忘的东西，条件指向将来会不会发生 → 一般现在时"]},{"id":"e03p2910","s":"Rex","t":"Well, I'll call you.","r":true},{"id":"e03p2911","s":"Bree","t":"Rex, in college, when we first started dating, people were so jealous of us.","r":true,"m":["college n. 大学，专科学校；学院，分院；公学；学会，社团；学院的全体师生","jealous adj. 妒忌的，好嫉妒的；珍惜的；猜疑的 be jealous of sb 嫉妒某人"]},{"id":"e03p2912","s":"Bree","t":"We were the golden couple, everybody knew we were going to have this wonderful life. Why is this happening?","r":true,"m":["the golden couple 金童玉女"]},{"id":"e03p2913","s":"Rex","t":"Because you can't even let me pack my own suitcase.","r":true,"m":["suitcase n. （旅行用的）手提箱，衣箱"]}]},{"id":"p30","title":"Susan 放下心结并收到 Brandi 的道歉","lines":[{"id":"e03p3001","s":"Julie","t":"Where are you going?","r":true},{"id":"e03p3002","s":"Susan","t":"Just a sec. Don't worry, I'm not packing heat. Hey, Brandi, would you scoot a little? Just scoot, thank you.","r":true,"m":["Just a sec 稍等 == just a second","pack heat 携带枪支；暗藏武器 heat n. 热能，热量；炎热，高温","scoot vi. 溜走；快走；骑轻便摩托车 scoot a little 挪开一点"]},{"id":"e03p3003","s":"Carl","t":"What are you doing?","r":true},{"id":"e03p3004","s":"Susan","t":"I'll be quick. Brandi, I'm sorry for the way I treated you. It was uncalled-for and childish, and it won't happen again.","r":true,"m":["I'll be quick 我长话短说 / 不会耽误你太久","uncalled-for 不必要的；无端的 uncalled adj. 未经邀请的；未被要求的","childish adj. 孩子的，孩子般的；幼稚的，孩子气的"]},{"id":"e03p3005","s":"Susan","t":"I have built up a lot of anger towards you, both of you. And I realize now that I just can't carry that around anymore, so apology or no apology, I'm moving on.","r":true,"m":["build up 积累, 增强, 逐渐发展","towards sb 朝着某人；对某人（来说）；关于某人","carry sth around 随身携带,背负着 be burdened with 偏向被施加"]},{"id":"e03p3006","s":"Carl","t":"Brandi, get in the car.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3007","s":"Brandi","t":"Mrs. Mayer.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3008","s":"Susan","t":"Please, call me Susan.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3009","s":"Brandi","t":"I just wanted you to know what happened between me and Carl, things got out of hand, because I thought your marriage was over. Anyway, I just wanted you to know I'm sorry, I really am.","r":true,"m":["I really am. 我真的是"]},{"id":"e03p3010","s":"Susan","t":"Thank you.","r":false},{"id":"e03p3011","s":"Alice","t":"And though it came from an unexpected source, Susan finally got the apology she'd always wanted.","r":true,"m":["unexpected adj. 想不到的，意外的","source n. 来源，出处；（问题的）原因，根源；"]}]},{"id":"p31","title":"Tom 为 Lynette 准备惊喜","lines":[{"id":"e03p3101","s":"Tom","t":"Hey, let me take those.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3102","s":"Lynette","t":"You're wearing a really big hat.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3103","s":"Tom","t":"Yes, I am. Listen, the kids are watching a video, which means that we've got only about 45 minutes until they actually find Nemo. So I suggest that we make the most of it.","r":true,"m":["video 视频、录像 audio 音频","radio 广播、收音机 radiation area 辐射区域 共同意象都是从中心向外发散的线——radio 发的是信号，radiation 发的是能量。","Nemo 尼莫:电影《海底总动员》Finding Nemo里的主角","make the most of it 充分利用最大价值或潜力，尽可能地从中获得利益或利润"]},{"id":"e03p3104","s":"Lynette","t":"By reliving your night out with the guys?","r":true,"m":["relive vt. 再体验 vi. 复活；再生","night out 外出玩乐的夜晚；夜晚外出消遣"]},{"id":"e03p3105","s":"Tom","t":"Lynette, I'm trying.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3106","s":"Lynette","t":"You look ridiculous in that thing.","r":true,"m":["ridiculous adj. 可笑的，荒谬的","in that thing 表示穿着或戴着某件物品，用 thing 而不用 dress 是因为说话人拒绝承认那是件正经衣服"]},{"id":"e03p3107","s":"Tom","t":"Sexy ridiculous?","r":true,"m":["sexy adj. 性感的"]},{"id":"e03p3108","s":"Lynette","t":"Maybe.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3109","s":"Tom","t":"I can live with maybe.","r":true,"m":["live with (sth) 接受并共处（不完美 / 不确定 / 现状）I can live with that.那我能接受"]},{"id":"e03p3110","s":"Lynette","t":"You know, it's gonna take more than just this one night.","r":true,"m":["It's gonna take more than... 这将需要不止……；这要花费比…… 更多的（时间、精力、金钱等）","this one night 这一夜"]},{"id":"e03p3111","s":"Tom","t":"I know. Looks like we have an audience.","r":true,"m":["audience 是集合名词，一个观众群 audiences（复数）指的是多批不同的观众群"]},{"id":"e03p3112","s":"Lynette","t":"Let them look, as long as they don't try and cut in.","r":true,"m":["as long as 只要，在……的时候，只要……就","try and do = try to do","cut in 打断，插嘴，插队"]}]},{"id":"p32","title":"Bree 发现 Alice 的录音带","lines":[{"id":"e03p3201","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Bree, we're not scheduled now, are we?","r":true,"m":["schedule v. 安排，预定； n. 计划（表），进度表；用被动语态表示某项活动没有被排进日程表"]},{"id":"e03p3202","s":"Bree","t":"I didn't have time to make an appointment. Rex moved out today.","r":true,"m":["make an appointment 预约 appointment n. 约会，约定；任命，委派"]},{"id":"e03p3203","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"I'm very sorry to hear that, but unfortunately, I'm completely booked right now.","r":true,"m":["unfortunately adv. 不幸地，遗憾地；","completely adv. 完全地，彻底地","book v. 预订，预约 n. 书，书籍；本子，簿册"]},{"id":"e03p3204","s":"Bree","t":"I don't need much time, it just seems that you have more insight into my situation than I do, and I just think...","r":true,"m":["it seems that/like 看起来……/似乎……","insight n. 洞悉，了解；洞察力 have insight into sth.对……有深入了解"]},{"id":"e03p3205","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"We can't talk now.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3206","s":"Bree","t":"If you could just tell me what he told you, then I could fix the problem.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3207","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"I can't do that, it's completely unethical.","r":true,"m":["unethical adj. 不道德的，不合乎道德标准的"]},{"id":"e03p3208","s":"Bree","t":"Why can't you ...","r":false},{"id":"e03p3209","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"That's my next appointment, you really need to go.","r":true},{"id":"e03p3210","s":"Bree","t":"Dr. Goldfine, please.","r":false},{"id":"e03p3211","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Hold on, I'll go and talk to my client.","r":true,"m":["Hold on 等待，坚持，紧握住","client n. 客户，委托人；客户机，用户端"]},{"id":"e03p3212","s":"Alice","t":"Bree searched for Rex's audiotape hoping to find answers, she found answers alright, but to entirely different questions.","r":true,"m":["search for sth 寻找某物；搜寻某物","audiotape n. 录音带 videotape n. 录像带","entirely adv. 完全地，完整地；仅仅，只","the answer to a question 固定搭配：某个问题的答案"]},{"id":"e03p3213","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"I understand completely, I'll be out in just a minute.","r":false,"m":["in a minute 在很短的时间内；很快"]},{"id":"e03p3214","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Bree, I'm sorry, he can't wait. But I can see you first thing in the morning, eight o'clock.","r":true,"m":["first thing in the morning常用表达，一大早；早上的第一件事"]},{"id":"e03p3215","s":"Bree","t":"Eight o'clock, sorry to interrupt, bye.","r":true,"m":["intrude：场合介入；interrupt：打断进程、说话；disturb：扰乱安宁。"]},{"id":"e03p3216","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, I remember the world -- every detail, and what I remember most is how afraid I was. What a waste.","r":true,"m":["What a waste (it is) 真浪费；太浪费了 How wasteful it is!"]},{"id":"e03p3217","s":"Alice","t":"You see, to live in fear is not to live at all.","r":true,"m":["to live in fear is not to live at all 生活在恐惧之中根本不算是生活。","to do is to do 的对称结构表达 A本质上等于B"]},{"id":"e03p3218","s":"Alice","t":"I wish I could tell this to those I left behind, but would it do any good? Probably not.","r":true,"m":["I wish + 过去式(could) 虚拟语气：与现在事实相反的愿望 I wish + 过去完成时：与过去相反 I wish + would：抱怨将来想改变的事","do good 固定搭配：有用、有好处","Would it do any good? 做了能有什么用处吗？（暗含怀疑：恐怕没用）"]},{"id":"e03p3219","s":"Alice","t":"I understand now, there will always be those who face their fears, and there will always be those who run away.","r":true,"m":["there will always be 总会有；总是会存在","face one's fears 面对某人的恐惧；直面自己的恐惧","run away 逃跑，离家出走，或者是逃脱"]}]}]};
